      "summary": "Cardrona Alpine Resort is open for skiing today, with a delayed opening after an intense blizzard passed through the resort and access road overnight. 15 cm of new snow fell in the past 24 hours and was still falling as the storm cleared, holding the natural base at 112 cm; it's currently -7°C with winds around 37 km/h gusting to 71 km/h, with snow showers forecast to clear by evening and strong southwest winds continuing. It's a storm-riding day for the enthusiasts, so wrapping up warm is essential. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall's Chondola, Whitestar Express and Valley View are all open; Captains Express is delayed pending avalanche mitigation work, with the T-Bar on hold and Soho Express, Willow's Quad and Wells Pipe Platter all closed; 5 of 10 lifts are currently running. Lifts may be affected by wind holds through the day. The access road is open with chains required on 2WD vehicles from Chain Bay 1, and an active road hazard advisory in place. The spring Pines Shuttle and bus schedule begins 1 October. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 5 / 10 Runs Open 0 / 38 Percent open 0 %",
