      "summary": "Treble Cone is open for skiing today, closing day of the season, with Home Basin open under a mixed bag of conditions — some firmness beneath fresh snow, with a few nice turns to be found, and the resort still in the cloud with light snow pulsing on and off. There's been 8 cm of new snow in the past 24 hours, with the natural base at 150 cm at the top of Home Basin; it's currently -6°C with winds around 27 km/h gusting to 51 km/h, expected to gradually clear into a nicer afternoon. Saddle Basin remains on hold pending weather improvement and avalanche control work, uncertain whether it opens today. Home Basin Express and the Beginner Platter are open, 2 of 3 lifts running, with the Saddle Quad on hold; 6 of 10 terrain zones are open including Home Basin, Powder Bowl and Matukituki Basin, with Saddle Basin and Summit Slopes on hold and Motatapu Chutes closed. The access road is graded and chain-free, though all vehicles must still carry chains; the top carpark is closed while the grader clears snow, with a free shuttle available for those without chains. Lifts & terrain Lifts Open 2 / 3 Runs Open 0 / 59 Percent open 0 %",
